# Windows batch files must keep CRLF endings. cmd.exe mis-parses an LF-only
# batch file — it drops the first character or two of a line, so `setlocal`
# runs as `tlocal` and `rem` as `m`. It fails loudly but confusingly, and it
# depends on the cloner's core.autocrlf, so pin it here rather than hope.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Keep prepared PDF bytes intact across Windows checkouts.
public/demo/*.pdf binary
